# Keep the build context small and reproducible — never copy build outputs, deps, or secrets.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/TestResults/

# The API's wwwroot is a git-committed convenience copy for local `dotnet run`. The image build
# always regenerates the SPA fresh (see Dockerfile web stage) — never let this stale, pre-built
# copy enter the API publish stage, or dotnet publish bakes its old hash-named assets into the
# image layer permanently (a later `rm -rf` can't undo it — Trivy's secret scan reads layer
# history, not just the final merged filesystem).
services/api/src/ServiceHub.Api/wwwroot/

# Local secrets & environment overrides (must never enter an image)
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.user
.env
.env.*
!apps/web/.env.production

# VCS / tooling / editor
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.venv/
**/.DS_Store

# Docs & private material — not needed to build or run the app
docs/
docs-private/
self-hosting/
deploy/
azuredevops/
*.md
!README.md

# Local data
**/servicehub-namespaces.json
**/*.db
